lines=['## Final design point (lossless frontend, measured bit cell)','',f"Frozen source snapshot **{c['final_snapshot_utc']}**; report {r['updated_utc']}.",'', '**The smallest screened one-die outline is25 ×31 mm with the assumed12 µm²/bit memory, which requires a smaller foundry bit cell than the open GF180 one. Using the measured open bit cell at assumed70% array efficiency needs29 ×31 mm and misses the assumed26 ×33 mm field under this packing policy. The option using existing open SRAM macros and no numerical change fits two25 ×29 mm dies.** All four outlines pass abstract placement, VDD/VSS connectivity and combined IR below5% under the stated assumed loads. The lossless frontend storage finding removes the previous numerical re-quantization requirement; it does not implement or time the decoder, complete array macro, shared buses, links or functional pad signals. Real workload power remains unmeasured.','', '### Exact native frontend representation','', '**`frontend_native_int8_lossless` uses2,090,240 B**:2,073,600 INT8 weight bytes +12,800 FP32 scale/offset bytes +3,840 unchanged bias bytes, replacing8,298,240 expanded FP32 ROM bytes. The lead-verified `accuracy-int8/existing-affine-int8-exact/manifest.json` records bit-for-bit reconstruction of all2,074,560 ROM coefficients. W3 independently verified every payload file size and SHA256 in [lossless_payload_audit.json](lossless_payload_audit.json). This is the original model encoding, with no changed numerical weights and no new accuracy-revalidation requirement.','', 'The decode contract is **round(INT8→FP32 × FP32 scale) to FP32, then add the FP32 offset with another FP32 rounding**. Conv2 uses input-channel axis1. A single fused multiply-add can differ and is not assumed equivalent. The area model counts **one FP32 multiply-add resource** within the existing **12 mm² ASSUMED frontend logic allowance**. A FMA-class unit must execute separate multiply/add modes or two separately rounded operations; the implementation, scheduling and throughput are unverified. No extra area or power saving is inferred for arithmetic; the frontend still carries the prior0.15 W assumed load. Biases bypass reconstruction.','', '**Symmetric re-quantized INT8 is not used.** W7’s per-channel scheme failed the ≤2 percentage-point degradation gate (clean+2.4242 pp; other+4.6154 pp). Per-tensor also failed, with100% WER in each condition. Those failures and the exact source-encoding finding are different experiments; earlier sections retain the history, while this final point uses only the bit-exact source representation.','', '### Measured SRAM cell and memory scenarios','', 'W3 reopened a copied official512×8 SRAM GDS with KLayout and measured `018SRAM_cell1_512x8m81` at **3.68 ×5.18 µm =19.0624 µm²** and `018SRAM_cell1_2x_512x8m81` at **3.68 ×9.68 µm =35.6224 µm² per pair**, or **17.8112 µm²/bit** before straps. The planning pitch rounds this to17.8 µm²/bit. Source/hash/bounding boxes are in [sram_bitcell_measurement.json](sram_bitcell_measurement.json); GDS SHA256 is `40d76d3ccfc8779c9db9f1db7a0bbccbbaf12c4627a3fa5b59049f23eef7d915`.','', '| Scenario | Effective density / basis | Final block area mm² |','|---|---|---:|']
